A||||4||PAWPAW||86 GT Front End Inner Tie Rods
Z||000000||PAWPAW||07-21-99||07:52 PM||||Has anyone replaced the inner tie rod ends?  What tools are  required to replace them?  My right front wheel has excessive play.  The joint at the rack and pinon has up and down movement with the rest solid.    <br>
Z||000001||theogre||07-22-99||01:26 PM||||the inner ends are considered part of the rack unit. Generally if they are gone it's time to do major work on the rack or replace it. I don't recomend tearing the rack apart unless you know what you're doing.... the tolerances are very particular.<p>If you can even get the rods as a seperate part, sometimes you can, then it's a matter of finding wrenches that fit. Don't use a pipe wrench or anything like it. The teeth can cause damage that could end up as stress cracks. Be very carefull with the boot, or you'll wreck it.
Z||000002||PAWPAW||07-25-99||08:17 PM||||The lcoal Auto parts places have both the outer and inner tie rod ends for replacement.  I have extensive movement at the right tie rod near the rack system causing wheel movement and frontend vibration.  I thought only the inner tie rod end needs replacement  Is replacement of the rack expensive?  I have  not priced the pieces parts  lately.    
Z||000003||batboy||07-25-99||09:34 PM||||A good front end shop that knows what they're doing can replace the inner tie rods. The average shade tree mechanic doesn't usually have to equipment or expertise to do it. I've seen it done before, but no way I'd tackle it by myself.
Z||000004||PAWPAW||07-26-99||04:47 PM||||Thanks for all the info. and advise.    I normally do all my own work but even the books do not address this work.
